  "notes": {
    "part:C1": "5 nF into a low input impedance (about 12 kΩ): a high-pass near 2.6 kHz, which makes it a treble booster. A bigger cap boosts more of the range.",
    "part:R1": "R1 and R2 set the base near -1 V. Builders swap R2 for a 100k trimmer to put the collector at -7 V with their transistor.",
    "part:VR1": "The volume pot is the collector load: DC runs through it, so it can scratch when turned.",
    "part:Q1": "Try your own transistor's measured hFE and leakage here: the collector moves with both."
  },
